;;;; z-ed-output.expected-failures.lisp
;;;;
;;;; Known failures for the deftests generated from
;;;; z-ed-output.test.
;;;;
;;;; Initially auto-generated by
;;;;   (fortran-format::establish-baseline-expected-failures ...)
;;;; but maintained by hand thereafter: remove a name when its
;;;; bug is fixed.
;;;;
;;;; The 175 entries below are all (Zw) tests of small negative
;;;; values at widths 8-10.  The corpus was captured on a 32-bit
;;;; gfortran 4.4.1, so it expects 32-bit two's-complement output:
;;;; -1 -> "FFFFFFFF" (8 hex digits), which fits Z8/Z9/Z10.
;;;;
;;;; When *boz-word-bits* is 64 we emit the 64-bit form
;;;; "FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF" (16 hex digits), which overflows widths
;;;; 8-10 and produces "*"s -- semantically correct for a 64-bit
;;;; Fortran compiler but mismatched against the captured corpus.
;;;;
;;;; B and O tests don't show this divergence because their corpus
;;;; widths (up to 10) overflow with either 32-bit or 64-bit
;;;; representations of small negatives.

